course: dictionary
lesson: 8671
title: Parts and sections
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A section is one part of something that has been split into parts. Read the context: «Each centipede has one pair of legs on each body section.» A centipede's body is made of parts joined together, and each part is a section.
explain: A section can also be a part of a group or a place. «So they piled cushions on the floor and called it the VIP section, and suddenly everyone wanted it.» The VIP section is one area of a bigger room, not a new room of its own.
explain: Musicians use sections too. «Musicians stop at the tricky bar (a small section of the music), play it slowly and correctly, then join it back in.» The clue is in the brackets: the bar is a small part of the whole piece.
explain: A cross-section is different. It is what you see when you cut straight through something. Cut a tree trunk across and the cross-section shows its rings. Look for the word cut, and you will often find the meaning.
fact: A section is one part of something that has been split into parts.
fact: A section can also be a part of a group or place, such as the sports section.
fact: «Section» can be used in maths: a whole can be split into equal sections, so whole = sections × size.
fact: A cross-section is what you see when you cut straight through something.
fact: «The Ming rebuilt and greatly extended walls in brick and stone, including the famous sections at Badaling and Mutianyu.»
exercise: Each centipede has one pair of legs on each body «section». What is a section here? | A type of cloud | A loud sound made by a bell | *A part of something split into parts | A kind of shoe
exercise: What do you see in a cross-section of a tree trunk? | Its flowers | *Its rings | Its roots | Its leaves
exercise: In «the reading section of a test», what does section mean? | A loud bell that ends the test | The end of the school day | A pencil used for writing | *The part of the test about reading
test: In «the children's section of the library», what does section mean? | A part of a place | A library card | *A part of a place, like one area of the library | A quiet rule for readers
test: A pizza is cut into 4 equal «sections». What is each section? | The whole pizza | A pizza box | A slice with no topping | *One equal part of the whole pizza
exam: In «the string section of the orchestra», what does section mean? | A type of string | A loud noise | *A part of a group of musicians | A piece of wood
